WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.940
We have a lot of choices
to make about our diet.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.820
Add to that, doing
the right thing

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.960
when it comes
to preventing

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.340
and treating a
chronic disease,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.620
fighting a virus,
or losing weight,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.080
and suddenly our
nutrition choices

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.420
can seem almost
overwhelming.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.880
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.200
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.600
Today we discuss
a condition

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.360
that we might not
even know we have

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.660
until someone is brave
enough to tell us:

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.771
bad breath.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.600
The word halitosis is derived
from the Latin and Greek terms

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.760
for abnormal or diseased breath,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.640
though it may be
less of a medical term

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.320
and more of a marketing term,

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.800
as it was supposedly coined
by the Listerine Company.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.120
Halitosis is commonly
referred to as bad breath,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.640
though medical and dental
professionals often use

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.720
instead of bad breath, the
less judgy term, breath odor.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.780
As described in the
Journal of Breath Research,

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.140
halitosis has been
classified into four types.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.980
There is genuine halitosis,
either transient or chronic,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.560
which is contrasted
with pseudo-halitosis,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.600
when someone thinks
they have bad breath,

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.420
but it’s evidently all in
their head, and

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.800
halitophobia, where they start
out with genuine halitosis,

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.600
but then they treat it,
and get rid of it,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.300
but still think they have it.
These are rare, though.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.440
The vast majority of cases
are IOH, which stands for

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.820
intra-oral halitosis, bad breath
arising from inside the mouth,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.680
as opposed to lungs or stomach,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.260
and not just anywhere in
the mouth, but specifically,

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:42.240
in most cases, apparently coming
off the coating on the tongue.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.320
Most people have a tongue coating,
a grayish-white deposit

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.100
on the tongue, which is the
main cause of bad breath.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.660
Now, there are pathological
conditions like black hairy tongue,

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.440
whose symptoms may include
an unattractive appearance

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.920
of the tongue, which can
be caused by certain drugs,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.580
but the normal tongue coating
is just a thin, slightly moist,

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.820
whitish substance across the
upper surface of the tongue

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.820
composed of sloughed
tongue cells, bacteria,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.780
seepage from our blood supply,
and secretions from our gums

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.920
and postnasal area, like mucus
discharge from our sinuses

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.140
dripping onto the
back of our tongue.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.980
Those with gum disease tend to
have four times as much coating,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.800
in terms of the wet weight
scraped off the tongue

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.920
due to the migration of white
blood cells from periodontal

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.140
pus pockets onto
the tongue surface,

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.840
but even in people with
perfect dental hygiene,

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.620
food particles can get trapped
between all the little bumps

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.820
and cracks on the tongue and form
a thick bacterial biofilm coating.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.860
If we eat the right foods, though,
our mouth may be self-cleaning.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.160
Just the act of chewing
and swallowing foods

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.940
that actually need chewing
can cleanse off the tongue,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.880
leaving you with just the
normal, thin layer of coating,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.600
but fast food is engineered
to be eaten fast.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.560
It’s soft, you can just gulp
it down and consequently,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.440
the thickness of the tongue
coating might increase,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.600
and that could
contribute to bad breath,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.160
but you don’t know... until
you put it to the test.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:22.020
“The effect of a chewing-intensive,
high-fiber diet on oral halitosis,”

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.800
a randomized clinical cross-
over study, in which subjects

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.140
were examined over
a period of 2.5 hours

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.340
after consumption of a
high-fiber vs. low-fiber meal

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.960
using an organoleptic
assessment of halitosis.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.640
Although a few electronic bad-breath
detectors have appeared

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.200
on the market, organoleptic scoring
is still the ‘gold standard,’

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.280
which is just a fancy name
for when dentists or doctors

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.260
just give your breath a sniff.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.160
Here’s the ratings they use:
no halitosis detected

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.780
even up close and personal,

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.740
or yeah, bad breath but only
up to about 4 inches away,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:06.360
or out to a foot, or all the
way out to more than a yard.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.620
We know halitosis is reduced by
eating, due to the “self-cleaning”

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.500
of the mouth while chewing
food, and it seems obvious

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.900
that foods that need to
be chewed more intensively

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.900
have a stronger self-cleaning
effect than foods

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.220
that require less chewing,

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.320
but whether this
is actually the case

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.680
had never been examined...
until now.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.820
The participants were randomized
to a high-fiber, high-chew meal

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.520
with a whole grain roll
with jam and a raw apple,

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.300
versus a low-fiber, low-chew
white bread roll with jelly

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.320
and a cooked apple and,
the result, a significantly

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.320
lower bad breath score immediately
after the high fiber meal

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.100
and then two-and-a-half hours
later compared to the low fiber meal.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.640
The researchers conclude that a
chewing-intensive, high-fiber meal

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:54.465
led to a greater
reduction of halitosis.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.180
Most bad breath is
due to the decay

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.040
of sulfur-containing
proteins.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.064
Here’s the story.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.500
It has been estimated
that 90 million Americans

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.780
or approximately 30 percent
of the U.S. population

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.740
currently suffers from bad
breath on a regular basis.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.100
And for those of you thinking “Phew,
I’m glad I’m not one of those,”

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.380
it is believed that
people with bad breath

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:19.800
can’t actually smell the odor
coming out of their own mouth.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.260
Maybe this is because
they’re just used to it,

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.180
or it’s because when you
sniff, you’re breathing air

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:27.780
from below rather than in
front where you’re exhaling.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.500
Either way, the mouth air of
chronic malodor sufferers

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.740
is tainted with compounds
such as hydrogen sulfide,

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.560
which produce a stream of
foul air that can be

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.200
gravely offensive to the
people in their vicinity.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.640
The characteristic smells
in halitosis include compounds

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.280
that smell like feces, like scatole,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.400
the rotten egg gas hydrogen sulfide,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:57.060
a corpse-like aroma from
cadaverine, a sweaty feet compound,

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:02.040
putrescine for the smell of
decaying meat, rotten cabbage,

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.120
rotten fish, pee, apples
don’t sound so bad,

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.200
and I don’t even know what
squashed bedbugs smell like.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:14.040
But, the major compounds that
contribute to oral malodor

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.760
are the VSCs, the
volatile sulfur compounds

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.320
such as hydrogen sulfide.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.560
Bacteria in our mouth,
predominantly on our tongue,

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.400
have the capacity to produce
these odorous sulfur compounds

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.720
through putrefaction of
sulfur-containing proteins.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.960
OK, so what can we do about it?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.400
Many have concentrated on trying
to reduce the bacterial load

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.340
in the mouth with like
antiseptic mouthwashes,

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.800
or finding ways to trap the VSCs.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:48.540
Mechanically, you can disrupt the
biofilm of bacteria on the tongue,

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.060
like with various tongue
scraping techniques,

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.700
though tongue cleaning
seems to work more through

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.400
reducing the substrates
for putrefaction,

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.320
rather than the
bacteria themselves.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.640
OK, but if the substrates
for VSC production

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.680
are the sulfur-containing
amino-acids,

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.860
and the sulfur-containing
amino acids are derived mainly

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.620
from animal protein, meat and dairy,

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.500
what about using a
dietary approach?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.940
The VSCs from animal protein
may actually explain why

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:21.720
carnivore poop smells so much
different than herbivore poop.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.740
And indeed, limiting the
amount of consumed proteins

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.100
may significantly reduce fetor ex ore,

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.440
from the Latin meaning
stench mouth.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.120
The reason they add fats and
alcohol is that they can both

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.600
cause relaxation of lower
esophageal sphincter.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:43.440
Normally, the only time you
exhale odors from your stomach

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.860
is when you burp, because the
sphincter at the top of the stomach

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.120
prevents stuff from backing up,
but alcohol or a fat-rich diet

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:54.180
increases the relaxation
of that sphincter,

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.900
which further increases the
risk and severity of bad breath.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.700
But most cases of halitosis occur
due to the decay of food residues

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.640
in the mouth by the bacteria
that decompose proteins and

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:09.300
amino acids and produces the
volatile sulfur compounds.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.720
So, the treatment of oral
halitosis should involve not just

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.020
professional advice on oral
hygiene, but also diet.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.920
Dairy proteins, for example, are
known to break down in the mouth

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.700
leading to the release of amino
acids that are rich in sulfur.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:27.840
Dairy products are rich sources
of the milk protein casein,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.680
and casein is rich in the sulfur-
containing amino acid cysteine,

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:36.000
which is a precursor to the
formation of the rotten egg gas

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.460
hydrogen sulfide in the oral cavity.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.820
In fact, that’s how you can
test people for bad breath.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.000
Cysteine challenge testing:
just have people

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.800
swish their mouth with it.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.200
When cysteine is degraded,
not only do you get

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.380
the hydrogen sulﬁde, which
comprises a large part

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.340
of the bad breath bouquet,
but you get sulfhydryl anions

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.820
that favor the growth of the
very bacteria within the mouth

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:03.600
responsible for the protein
putrefaction that’s central

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.900
to the production of oral
malodor in the first place

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.900
and to the development
of gum disease.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.620
So, it’s not just a one-two
punch, but a triple threat.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:16.680
Bad breath isn’t just
some aesthetic issue;

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.220
these volatile sulfur compounds
can be toxic to the gums,

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:23.340
even at extremely low concentrations.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:27.780
Hydrogen sulfide reacts
with collagen and can alter

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:31.020
the protein structure, thereby
rendering your gums and jaw

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:32.820
more susceptible to destruction.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.660
Then you can develop
these pockets of putrid pus

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.700
that can lead to more halitosis.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:42.300
The periodontal pockets
are the second main source

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.860
of the volatile sulfur compounds.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:46.380
Even people with mild periodontitis

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.740
may have twice the risk
of reporting bad breath.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.700
Finally, let me touch
on the role diet has

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.220
in so-called extra-oral halitosis,

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.860
bad breath that doesn’t
originate in the mouth.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.260
There are lots of
drugs that can do it,

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.360
including dietary
supplements like fish oil,

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:07.740
but there’s another way people
can smell fishy: trimethylamine.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.700
Trimethylaminuria is
one the largest causes

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.740
for undiagnosed body odor.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:17.340
It’s when you can’t sufficiently
metabolize a malodorous compound

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.040
called trimethylamine,
which is formed in your gut

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.360
when you eat lots of choline.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:25.140
The textbook presentation
is urine, breath, sweat,

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:29.520
and reproductive fluids smelling
like rotten or decaying fish,

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:33.720
but what many doctors don’t
realize is that the fish odor

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:37.200
presentation may only occur in
like 10 percent of individuals

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.520
who have this predisposition.

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:43.200
Yes, at high concentrations,
trimethylamine has a foul,

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.900
rotten fish odor, but
at low concentrations,

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:50.580
it can just give you kind of a
unpleasant garbage-like breath.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.660
And because there are many
foods that are rich in choline,

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.840
like the fact that there are
eggs found in so many foods,

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.380
you may not make the
connection between your diet

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:05.040
and your body odor, but you
can always try cutting out foods

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:09.662
like egg yolks for a few weeks
and see if you smell any better.

